the surly buffalo must give way to the formidable team. At the heart of this bond is the remarkable

00:18:58.870 --> 00:18:59.970
biology of

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:08.250
the cow. A cow can eat pretty much anything and miraculously transform it into milk, meat and a

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:15.550
whole range of other products that sustain our daily lives. The key to the cow's success lies

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:22.240
here, the rumen. It's the belief of every school child that the cow has four stomachs. That's not

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:27.140
really true. What it has is one true stomach, the abomasin, which is exactly the same as our stomach.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.960
Upstream of that is a mul...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.740
a multi-compartmental fermentation vat, fermentation chamber,

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:34.800
wherein live the microbes.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.780
Now, when the cow goes out to graze,

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.240
she eats the grass really as quickly as possible

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:41.800
and swallows it almost unchanged.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.060
That comes into the rumen, and at that point,

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.920
it's really quite difficult for the microbes

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.320
to penetrate through the cell wall

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:51.200
and start the chemical digestion of the plant fibre.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.300
So what the cow has also evolved

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.520
is this really elegant mechanism of rumination.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.910
In this, she moves the food round in the rumen.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:05.130
and then a bolus of food is regurgitated, passes up to the mouth,

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:08.560
and then she takes it in her mouth and chews it rather as...

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.370
Oh, cowboys would chew tobacco.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:12.530
20 chews on one side, 20 chews on the other.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.300
This breaks it up, and it comes back down again into the rumen.

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.240
The microbes, having done their work,

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:22.590
then are passed out of the fermentation chamber into the abomasin,

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:26.230
where they heroically die and give up their lives to provide protein for the cow

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:27.950
to produce milk and meat for ourselves.

