00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:07.040
Taking each day as it comes, urban zebu, the ancient humped cattle of India, have adapted

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:12.900
to graze not on grass, but on garbage, making do on a diet of discarded fruit and vegetable

00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:17.200
waste, or if need be, newspapers and cardboard boxes.

00:24:19.610 --> 00:24:23.610
Once again, the cow's miraculous stomach comes to its rescue.

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:29.970
With the help of the trillions of bacteria and billions more protozoa resident inside the

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:36.250
50-gallon rumen, the cow is able to ferment otherwise indigestible cellulose into vinegar,

00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:38.190
its primary source of energy.

00:24:39.200 --> 00:24:42.750
Just another everyday miracle in the life of the holy cow.

00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:49.510
But occasionally, even this ultimate survivor falls on such hard times that it needs our

00:24:49.510 --> 00:24:49.810
help.

00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:59.860
Enter Dr. Sardana Rao, who retired from medical practice to devote her whole life.

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:02.370
to the welfare of old and injured cattle.

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:11.060
She is the Mother Teresa of the bovine world,

00:25:11.570 --> 00:25:13.490
funding this hospice from her pension

00:25:13.640 --> 00:25:15.900
and whatever donations she receives.

00:25:16.650 --> 00:25:19.910
This place is actually a home for the abandoned,

00:25:20.310 --> 00:25:24.370
unwanted, old animals, mostly cows.

00:25:25.220 --> 00:25:29.900
I accept destitute, abandoned, sick, lame, blind, all animals.

00:25:31.500 --> 00:25:34.120
This one is completely blind. It was born blind.

00:25:34.590 --> 00:25:37.720
His name is Gopi. This fellow is Gopi.

00:25:43.200 --> 00:25:47.090
She is 23 years old. In this sense, she is the oldest cow.

00:25:47.660 --> 00:25:49.640
I want a cow which is 26 years old.

00:25:50.310 --> 00:25:52.790
There are no teeth there. We have to cut the grass.

00:25:52.910 --> 00:25:54.790
We have to give her only the softest thing.

00:25:56.620 --> 00:25:59.900
Some of Dr. Rao's charges have endured terrible suffering.

00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:04.780
These buffalo were caught in a fire in their stable and were rescued by Dr. Rao.

00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:09.240
That was three years ago, and she's still nursing them back to health.

00:26:10.430 --> 00:26:12.010
Hey, this one goes on licking.

00:26:12.210 --> 00:26:13.510
It doesn't allow me to do anything.

00:26:15.220 --> 00:26:15.720
Okay, ma'am.

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:21.530
You have to talk to them to make them feel at home so that even when they are in pain,

00:26:21.830 --> 00:26:25.580
even when they are in pain, if you are near them and if you talk to them,

00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:29.280
they get a kind of moral support and they're able to bear the pain.

00:26:31.660 --> 00:26:34.110
I cannot bear when they are unhappy.

00:26:34.430 --> 00:26:37.010
And I feel like a fish out of water

00:26:37.010 --> 00:26:39.080
when I'm not in the midst of cows.

00:26:41.620 --> 00:26:44.460
Dr. Rao knows each of her charges as an individual.

00:26:45.720 --> 00:26:47.380
His name is Ayipasami.

00:26:48.790 --> 00:26:49.900
Ayipa, for short.

00:26:50.140 --> 00:26:56.870
I feel very happy when I'm done.

00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:58.620
Completely fulfilled.

00:26:59.630 --> 00:26:59.910
What?

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:03.920
motivates someone to dedicate their whole life to the welfare of cows.

00:27:05.010 --> 00:27:09.560
God has sent me in this world only to serve them. That's what I think. I have no other

00:27:09.560 --> 00:27:15.740
explanation. The cow occupies a unique place in the religious life of India, where cattle

00:27:15.740 --> 00:27:23.220
are considered sacred. The divine bull Nandi guards Hindu temples, while the holy cow Karmadinu

00:27:23.380 --> 00:27:28.990
grants all human wishes. Together, they and their living incarnations are worshipped

00:27:28.990 --> 00:27:29.790
by 700

00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:31.190
50 million Hindus.

00:27:47.560 --> 00:27:49.960
As night falls, a cow goes into labor.

00:27:53.290 --> 00:27:58.270
It is a familiar nativity scene in tens of thousands of stables up and down this vast

00:27:58.270 --> 00:27:58.630
land.

00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:13.980
Just after midnight, her waters break.

00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:19.940
In the early hours, a calf is born.

00:28:25.110 --> 00:28:29.790
This is no ordinary morning, and therefore, this will be no ordinary calf.

00:28:31.470 --> 00:28:35.770
For today is Matu Pongal, India's bovine thanksgiving,

00:28:36.190 --> 00:28:38.430
when the cow's many gifts are celebrated.

00:28:46.600 --> 00:28:48.820
Matu Pongal begins at first light,

00:28:49.300 --> 00:28:51.280
after the farmers have washed their herds,

00:28:51.580 --> 00:28:53.440
the cattle are decorated and then fed

00:28:53.440 --> 00:28:54.740
ritually prepared food.

00:29:00.440 --> 00:29:06.710
On Matupongo, even street cattle help themselves freely from the local vegetable markets.

00:29:06.950 --> 00:29:26.440
For the street cows, today is a day of abundance in an otherwise tough existence.

00:29:26.440 --> 00:29:29.960
But our special calf is destined for a very...

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:35.260
life at the local temple. The calf's auspicious birthday ensures its

00:29:35.260 --> 00:29:45.360
privileged future. Its short journey will pass through thousands of years of

00:29:45.360 --> 00:29:46.020
living history.

00:30:05.760 --> 00:30:08.940
Contradictions are the foundation of everyday life here.

00:30:11.860 --> 00:30:15.780
Revered as sacred, the cow is also a lowly beast of burden,

00:30:16.250 --> 00:30:18.770
toils in the fields and provides daily transport.

00:30:26.950 --> 00:30:29.960
And fed, pampered, and decorated, the cow

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.320
is also abandoned to forage for itself in the streets.

00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:37.960
The cow is both a long-suffering animal

00:30:37.960 --> 00:30:40.920
and the infinitely adaptable mother of the universe.

00:30:45.540 --> 00:30:48.940
Even in the 21st century, a new building cannot begin

00:30:48.940 --> 00:30:50.910
without the holy cow's blessing.

00:30:51.240 --> 00:30:53.640
And when complete, the owners must perform

00:30:53.640 --> 00:30:55.280
the necessary bovine rituals.

00:30:57.210 --> 00:30:59.710
This is no backward village superstition.

00:31:00.350 --> 00:31:07.540
Attending this ceremony are modern professionals, a filmmaker, a doctor, an airline pilot, and a successful businessman.

00:31:08.740 --> 00:31:11.880
But without the cow's blessings, nobody can move in.

00:31:21.520 --> 00:31:28.070
If, to Western eyes, India seems a riddle, then the holy cow is surely her sphinx.

00:31:36.590 --> 00:31:38.630
The calf's journey ends at the temple.

00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:09.310
Within the goshala, the sacred stable, the calf will live out its life alongside other resident holy cows,

00:32:09.880 --> 00:32:14.870
acting as a focus of thanks for the many gifts which the cow has given to India.

00:32:39.720 --> 00:32:44.750
Cattle reflect the values of the cultures to which they belong, and in the West, the

00:32:44.750 --> 00:32:48.130
cow has adapted to suit the needs of a more secular society.

00:32:51.630 --> 00:32:56.440
In the rolling countryside of England, the cow would perform its most practical conjuring

00:32:56.440 --> 00:32:59.940
trick, literally changing shape to suit its masters.

00:33:03.320 --> 00:33:07.000
Although different types of cattle evolved in different parts of the world,

00:33:07.680 --> 00:33:12.940
it was in England in the 18th century that the story of cattle breeding really began.

00:33:14.260 --> 00:33:18.240
The names of British breeds record where they originated in the United Kingdom,

00:33:18.720 --> 00:33:23.860
and although a small island, the result has been over 40 different shapes and sizes.

00:33:25.500 --> 00:33:29.980
This is the English Longhorn, one of the oldest recognized breeds in the world.

00:33:30.540 --> 00:33:32.780
and the first bred purely for beef.

00:33:34.330 --> 00:33:36.800
The Highland, a hardy breed from Scotland,

00:33:37.040 --> 00:33:39.220
able to endure the most extreme conditions.

00:33:41.730 --> 00:33:43.920
The Gloucester, an early dairy breed,

00:33:44.320 --> 00:33:46.120
celebrated for producing cheese.

00:33:48.500 --> 00:33:51.220
Aberdeen Angus, renowned for meat production

00:33:51.220 --> 00:33:54.170
and the most popular beef breed in America today.

00:33:55.860 --> 00:33:58.210
The South Devon, the largest British breed.

00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:04.680
And finally, the Hereford, the most widespread and adaptable of all cattle.

00:34:11.650 --> 00:34:19.340
At Haven Farm in the heart of Herefordshire, the Lewis family have been successfully breeding pedigree Herefords for over 100 years.

00:34:20.420 --> 00:34:27.520
The first Hereford came from a farm a few miles down the road, and today there are 30 million of them from Alaska to New Zealand.

00:34:48.680 --> 00:34:54.360
Edward Lewis prepares to load two prize bulls, Volcano and Viking, for the annual pilgrimage

00:34:54.360 --> 00:34:57.380
to the Three Counties Agricultural Show at Malver.

00:35:04.600 --> 00:35:08.600
Success in the competition brings far more than just a winner's red rosette.

00:35:09.450 --> 00:35:14.990
Artificial insemination means that a champion can fertilize tens of thousands of cows in a lifetime.

00:35:15.980 --> 00:35:21.860
The very top pedigree bulls can earn their owners a million and a half dollars in stud fees a year.

00:35:25.690 --> 00:35:29.690
At the Malvern Showground, Edward Lewis' stockman settles in the bulls.

00:35:33.920 --> 00:35:38.770
Edward's son, Ben, will be the sixth generation to breed Herefords, following his father,

00:35:39.380 --> 00:35:46.590
grandfather and great-grandfather, in an unbroken line back to Thomas Lewis, the founder of

00:35:46.590 --> 00:35:47.010
the herd.

00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:54.320
The family's been involved since 1822, so yeah, long enough.

00:36:10.620 --> 00:36:23.680
The final washing, drying and brushing by the Lewis girls are just the last minute touches on years of preparation with decades of selection and breeding going into the presentation of the top pedigree animal.

00:36:24.680 --> 00:36:27.960
A lot of work got into them and it's sort of now and ever.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:45.150
they look anyway first the judge looks at the animal's locomotion its general

00:36:45.150 --> 00:36:51.080
structure color and markings next he assesses the combination of straight

00:36:51.080 --> 00:36:56.360
back the set of the shoulders well-made hindquarters and correct placing of the

00:36:56.360 --> 00:36:59.940
feet finally it's

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:05.200
overall size and the balance of muscle to fat that will determine meat production and

00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:14.540
decide the choice of champion. But the coveted red rosette goes to a rival. Edward comes

00:37:14.540 --> 00:37:22.360
in a respectable second with a blue. Although today is not the Lewis' day, they are sure

00:37:22.360 --> 00:37:27.520
to produce more champions. The Haven Farm has held the British sale record for the past

00:37:27.520 --> 00:37:28.260
20 years.

00:37:41.580 --> 00:37:47.000
Different cattle breeds reflect a combination of where they came from and what they are intended for.

00:37:47.770 --> 00:37:51.150
By exaggerating desirable characteristics through careful selection,

00:37:51.810 --> 00:37:57.830
man has created 800 different breeds with shapes and sizes never before seen in nature.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:04.320
plains of southern England or on the Great Plains of the States, the beef

00:38:04.320 --> 00:38:09.000
cattle have been selected by a man to produce beef. That's to say they have

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:14.100
short legs and vast amounts of meat all around them. So they've been selected by

00:38:14.100 --> 00:38:15.200
by the butcher, in essence.

00:38:15.560 --> 00:38:17.440
The winner of the Client Vegetable Trophy

00:38:17.440 --> 00:38:19.720
is the British Cimetal Champion,

00:38:20.200 --> 00:38:21.360
Sturgeon Frankacham.

00:38:23.150 --> 00:38:25.530
...Hoddington Stakes, Shelton and Gloucester.

00:38:26.720 --> 00:38:28.180
Thank you very much indeed. Thank you.

00:38:28.360 --> 00:38:28.980
Thank you.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:32.540
nearly 1,600 kilos of weight.

00:38:33.460 --> 00:38:35.200
Beef is only half the story,

00:38:35.220 --> 00:38:37.710
and now it's the turn of the dairy cattle

00:38:37.710 --> 00:38:38.730
at the Malvern show.

00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:42.700
Exhibiting his classic black and white Holstein Frisians

00:38:43.140 --> 00:38:45.680
is dairyman David Cale with his daughter Emma.

00:38:46.530 --> 00:38:49.270
What qualities will the judges be looking for this time?

00:38:50.030 --> 00:38:51.190
They've got great udders on them

00:38:51.190 --> 00:38:52.810
with what he's gonna be looking for.

00:38:53.090 --> 00:38:55.160
The teats are in the right place.

00:38:55.340 --> 00:38:56.560
The leg set is right.

00:38:56.700 --> 00:38:58.060
The openness of rib is right.

00:38:58.180 --> 00:38:59.820
The dairiness through the front end is right.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.440
Skin is even ripe.

00:39:02.210 --> 00:39:07.370
It's just what I think the modern-day Holstein breeder would thrive to try and breed, though, really.

00:39:07.790 --> 00:39:11.820
You have to try and figure out what time the cow's going to look her best.

00:39:12.020 --> 00:39:13.780
They were milked at 4 o'clock last night,

00:39:13.780 --> 00:39:19.220
so we believe that they're capable of carrying 17, 18 hours of milk to look their real best.

00:39:19.860 --> 00:39:22.980
Because at the end of the day, if we don't get those udders blooming like they should,

00:39:23.060 --> 00:39:27.080
and we don't get that udder filled right to the top, she won't win her class.

00:39:27.400 --> 00:39:29.980
In a dairy cow such as...

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:36.520
this is the factory. This is the udder where the milk is produced. In an Ayrshire cow in a very

00:39:36.520 --> 00:39:42.830
natural grazing environment such as this will at peak give about 50 or 60 pints a day which is

00:39:42.830 --> 00:39:51.190
about 12,000 pints in a lactation. And it is secreted in cells that live in the top part of

00:39:51.190 --> 00:39:56.410
the udder. Underneath that is a cistern which is as the name implies it's just a tank that holds

00:39:56.410 --> 00:39:59.900
the milk. The bottom of that we have the teat and the teat canal which remain.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:05.140
closed, for obvious reasons, until such time as either the calf comes to drink from its

00:40:05.140 --> 00:40:10.180
mother or she goes into the milking parlour. Then a hormone, oxytocin, is released from

00:40:10.180 --> 00:40:17.090
the brain, is carried in the bloodstream to the secretory cells of the udder and causes

00:40:17.810 --> 00:40:22.890
myoebithelial, specialised cells, to contract and squeeze the milk out of the secretory

00:40:22.890 --> 00:40:26.680
glands into the cistern and out through the teat canal.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.800
In the dairy breeds, milk production is what counts.

00:40:33.490 --> 00:40:34.850
Worthy when there's a last class.

